<meta type=article>
  <title | Multi-paragraph tag content fixture>
  <author | Test Author>
</meta>

<section | Aside with blank line in content>

The aside below contains a blank line in its content. Under Option A
(decided 2026-05-26), a blank line inside an open tag is a paragraph
break, not a terminator — the tag remains open until its explicit
closing `>`. The aside must produce two paragraph children.

<aside | First paragraph of the aside.

Second paragraph of the aside, after a blank line.>

This fixture pins Option A's allow-multi-paragraph-tag-content half
against regression. RC-6 in `remark-acadamark/test/test-recursive.js`
covers this at the parser level; this fixture covers the full
integration pipeline end-to-end.
